{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993993-mind-shield","id":993993,"title":"Mind Shield","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-27T05:26:03-07:00","id":993993,"title":"Mind Shield","content":"The book says: &quot;Meanwhile, the mage also learns to shield his own mind from the thoughts and emotions of other people, constructing mental barriers around his aura, emotions, and consciousness. Each success on a coincidental Arete roll removes one success from any other character\u2019s attempt to read those psychic elements. &quot;<br /> <br /> Does that mean that it protects you from any mental powers at all, like dominate etcetera from affecting you? or it only shields you from specific mind related powers such as mind reading etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T09:03:27-07:00","id":994051,"title":"","content":"The way I play it, it protects from any mental power, from reading minds, to mental domination (including the powers of Vampires, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T15:52:21-07:00","id":994253,"title":"","content":"I'd say all mental powers, regardless of source.<br /> <br /> Heck, in the case of Vampire Disciplines, it should be wider than first glance. Obfuscate and Chimestry are both Disciplines that affect the target's senses (it's actually not stated whether Chimestry illusions are purely &quot;mental&quot;, or if they count as &quot;physical&quot; illusions; Storytellers should use their judgment here), so Mind should be able to counter them. That said, it depends on which crossover rules we're running with here. Over in Vampire, it's a contested roll between Vampire and Mage (or other night folk) if the Vampires tries to pierce the other's illusions/invisibility. So presumably, the same would be true if the roles were reversed. Over here in Mage, though, Mind 1 protects against mostly everything. And then there are higher Mind powers, which can be used to weave false auras or thoughts in the Mage, which could fool specific applications of Auspex.<br /> <br /> Since we're here in the Mage forum, we'll assume we're working with Mage-biased crossover rules. (For the record, there are no crossover rules that aren't biased towards one of the splats over the others. That's just how the Classic World of Darkness rolls.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T19:51:09-07:00","id":994354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MowtekPvP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993993-mind-shield#post993993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book says: &quot;Meanwhile, the mage also learns to shield his own mind from the thoughts and emotions of other people, constructing mental barriers around his aura, emotions, and consciousness. Each success on a coincidental Arete roll removes one success<b> from any other character\u2019s attempt to read those psychic elements</b>. &quot;<br /> <br /> Does that mean that it protects you from any mental powers at all, like dominate etcetera from affecting you? or it only shields you from specific mind related powers such as mind reading etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, that clearly means that it only burns off successes from Disciplines that read aspects of you, like aura reading or telepathy. You could probably work a spell that adjusted the difficulty to affect you with a mental discipline by up to 3 points at Mind 1, or one that adjusted the difficulty of your roll to resist by up to 3 points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}